  "identity": "Leiden University, RIO 59320, ordinary full-time English BSc, September 2026 basis.",
  "curriculum": "BA-BASS 2261 catalogue tree and 20 exact current modules reconcile to 60+60+60 EC with unique component codes. The adopted OER §§2.2, 2.4–2.6, 2.9 and 3.1–3.2 confirms ordinary English full-time study, no specialisations, 150 EC compulsory and 30 EC student-selected. The required year-three components total 30 EC. The current minor is separately listed under 4000MCSGEN and grounds the digital option without filling the comparator elective space.",
  "progression": "OER §§3.1–3.2 and §6.3 and the official programme structure describe elective approval and the first-year 45 EC binding study advice (subject to formal exceptions). Individual modules 8913302Y and 8913380Y require passing Integrated Project 1 before Integrated Project 2 and all 60 first-year EC plus at least 45 second-year EC and a complete research-methods sequence before the thesis. For this curriculum the sequence is Introduction, Quantitative and Qualitative Research Methods. The 30 EC elective module specifies semester one of year three. The skills labs and methods courses build sequentially; no additional hard entry conditions were inferred from recommended sequencing.",
